  "definition": "A Sun-synchronous orbit (SSO) is an Earth orbit whose orbital plane precesses at approximately the same mean rate that the Sun appears to move around Earth, about 0.9856 degrees per day. This keeps the plane at an approximately fixed orientation to the Sun and gives successive observations at a controlled local solar time.[^1]",
